# Deployment configuration for deploy.sh.
#
#   cp .env.example .env    then set PROJECT_ID.
#
# There are no credentials in this file. DATABASE_URL, the transcoder callback
# token, and the admin token are generated inside GCP on the first deploy and
# stored in Secret Manager; Cloud Run reads them at runtime. Nothing sensitive
# is written to disk, so there is nothing here to leak.
#
# .env is gitignored and excluded from the Docker and Cloud Build contexts.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------

# The GCP project to deploy into. Must already exist and have billing enabled.
#   gcloud projects list
PROJECT_ID=vibetube-streaming-platform

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Defaults apply if these are left unset; uncomment to override.

# REGION=us-central1

# Cloud SQL machine type. db-f1-micro and db-g1-small are shared-core, so a
# busy event may be throttled on either; db-n1-standard-1 is the first tier
# with a dedicated vCPU. The tier also determines max_connections, which must
# stay above MAX_INSTANCES x DB_POOL_MAX (10 x 5 = 50 by default).
# DB_TIER=db-g1-small

# Resource names. Buckets default to <PROJECT_ID>-raw-videos and
# <PROJECT_ID>-public-streams, since bucket names are globally unique and
# deriving them from the project keeps two deployments from colliding.
# Set these only when adopting resources that already exist under other names.
# REPO_NAME=vibetube
# DB_INSTANCE_NAME=vibetube-db-instance
# DB_NAME=vibetube
# RAW_BUCKET=
# PUBLIC_BUCKET=
# JOB_NAME=transcoder-job
# SERVICE_NAME=vibetube-service

# Secret Manager entry names. Change these only to adopt secrets that already
# exist -- the values themselves are never set here.
# SECRET_DATABASE_URL=vibetube-database-url
# SECRET_TRANSCODER_TOKEN=vibetube-transcoder-token
# SECRET_ADMIN_TOKEN=vibetube-admin-token

# Cloud Run runtime service account. Defaults to the project's compute default.
# RUNTIME_SA=

# Admin console allowlist seed, comma-separated. These addresses are inserted
# into the admin_users table on first start so a fresh deployment can be
# administered; everything after that is managed in the console's Admins panel.
# The seed only ever ADDS -- removing someone in the console is not undone by a
# redeploy.
#
# The Firebase web config (API key, auth domain) is NOT set here: deploy.sh
# reads it back from the Firebase project so there is one source of truth.
# ADMIN_BOOTSTRAP_EMAILS=weimeilin@gmail.com,linchr@google.com

# Cloud Run scale ceiling. Raising this without raising the database tier is
# how you get connection-exhaustion errors under load.
# MAX_INSTANCES=10

# --- Content screening -------------------------------------------------------
# Uploads are screened on two surfaces before they reach the room: Gemini on
# Vertex watches the video inside the transcoder job, and Model Armor screens
# the text the submitter typed (title, description, name, ad copy). deploy.sh
# enables both APIs, grants the runtime service account access, and creates the
# Model Armor template.
#
# Off switch. Screening is on by default wherever GCP_PROJECT is set; local
# runs have no Vertex endpoint and skip it regardless.
# MODERATION_ENABLED=true

# The model that watches the video. A variable because model ids move faster
# than this repo is redeployed.
# MODERATION_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# What happens when screening cannot reach a verdict -- Vertex down, quota
# exhausted past the retry budget, a malformed response.
#
# Defaults to false, meaning fail-open: the video is published unscreened and
# the reason is logged. That is the right default for a live workshop, where a
# Vertex outage silently blocking every upload in the room is worse than a few
# unscreened videos in a room the organisers are watching. Set true for an
# unattended deployment.
# MODERATION_FAIL_CLOSED=false

# 429 handling for the video scan, which runs in the background job. Ten
# attempts thirty seconds apart is a five-minute ceiling; it has to stay inside
# JOB_TIMEOUT (20m) with room left for the encode.
# MODERATION_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=10
# MODERATION_RETRY_INTERVAL=30

# 429 handling for the text scan, which runs inside the upload request and so
# gets a much smaller budget -- the job's 10 x 30s would exceed Cloud Run's
# 300s request timeout and hang the upload. Raise only alongside that timeout.
# MODERATION_TEXT_RETRY_ATTEMPTS=3
# MODERATION_TEXT_RETRY_INTERVAL=5

# The Model Armor template holding the text filter thresholds. Created by
# deploy.sh when missing; tune the thresholds in the console afterwards.
# MODEL_ARMOR_TEMPLATE=vibetube-text

# Replaces the video screening policy wholesale, for tuning a particular event
# without rebuilding the transcoder image. Set on the JOB rather than here:
#   gcloud run jobs update transcoder-job --region us-central1 \
#     --update-env-vars "MODERATION_POLICY=..."
# MODERATION_POLICY=
